# Log rotation for project-mai-tai.
#
# Retention is 30 daily rotations, derived from the longest evidence-discovery
# delay observed by 2026-08-24: the question reached back to 2026-08-03 (21
# days).  Thirty days preserves that population with nine days of margin.
#
# This is deliberately the COMPLETE application log population, not a marker
# allowlist.  The questions are discovered after the event; an allowlist would
# silently discard any marker, traceback, or surrounding context omitted from
# the second schema.
#
# Storage measurement on 2026-08-25: 53 MB total application logs, including
# only 6.3 MB of compressed rotations, with 88 GB free on the VPS.  Thirty days
# is therefore bounded and inexpensive under the observed workload.  The
# 200 MB early-rotation threshold remains (it is evaluated when logrotate runs;
# it is not an intraday hard cap).
#
# copytruncate is required because systemd StandardOutput=append holds the open
# inode.  Rename/create would leave the service writing to the rotated file.

/var/log/project-mai-tai/*.log {
    daily
    rotate 30
    maxsize 200M
    copytruncate
    compress
    delaycompress
    missingok
    notifempty
    dateext
    su root root
    create 0640 root root
}
